KW  - Non-destructive evaluation
KW  - Concrete bridge deterioration
KW  - Automated defect detection
KW  - Instance segmentation
KW  - Vision–language modeling
KW  - Metaheuristic optimization
KW  - Condition assessment
AB  - Timely and reliable assessment of concrete deterioration is critical for ensuring the safety and serviceability of bridge structures, yet conventional visual inspections remain labor-intensive, subjective, and difficult to standardize. Current artificial intelligence (AI)-based methods often lack the fine-grained quantification and domain-specific reporting required for reliable cost estimation. This study proposes a non-destructive evaluation framework that integrates computer vision with multimodal large language models (MLLMs) to automate the detection, quantification, and documentation of concrete bridge defects. A You Only Look Once (YOLO)11-seg instance segmentation model, fine-tuned using the Pilgrimage Walk Optimization (PWO) algorithm, identifies and classifies five concrete deterioration types. Pixel-level masks are further used to quantify defect areas for condition assessment and repair cost estimation. In parallel, a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)–enhanced language model, fine-tuned with Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) for parameter-efficient training, generates component-specific inspection descriptions and standardized repair recommendations in accordance with engineering guidelines. Experimental results demonstrate that PWO enhances segmentation performance compared with baseline training, and Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers Score (BERTScore) analysis confirms strong semantic alignment between generated and reference reports. By coupling metaheuristic optimization with retrieval-grounded language generation, the framework enhances the precision, consistency, and reproducibility of concrete deterioration evaluation. The proposed framework provides a practical tool for automated condition evaluation, engineering documentation, and maintenance decision-making in bridge inspection workflows.
ER  - 

