T1  - VibeFlow: An intelligent CFD workflow framework based on unified source-of-truth and dynamic parameter heuristics
AU  - Hao, Jiangxu
AU  - Xie, Bin
AU  - Liao, Shijun
JO  - Journal of Ocean Engineering and Science
SP  - 100783
PY  - 2026
DA  - 2026/11/14/
SN  - 2468-0133
DO  - https://doi.org/10.1016/j.joes.2026.100783
UR  - https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2468013326001944
KW  - Computational fluid dynamics
KW  - Large language model
KW  - Simulation automation
KW  - AI4Science
KW  - OpenFOAM
AB  - This paper presents VibeFlow, an intelligent workflow framework for managing the complete lifecycle of computational fluid dynamics research. At its core, VibeFlow introduces a centralized case definition file, caseDict, serving as the single source of truth for every project stage. It persistently stores user objectives, physical assumptions, geometric parameters, mesh requirements, numerical configurations, post-processing evidence, and report conclusions, ensuring all decisions and artifacts remain traceable. Built upon this unified foundation, VibeFlow integrates two complementary operational modes within a single agent-based harness. The usage mode guides a case from initial requirement elicitation through parametric geometry construction, mesh generation, numerical simulation, post-processing, and final report compilation. The development mode supports creating, compiling, and validating user-defined functions, solver extensions, boundary conditions, and post-processing utilities, enabling seamless transition from code development to case execution. To address the inherent incompleteness of natural language requirements, VibeFlow incorporates a dynamic parameter heuristic that intelligently prioritizes missing parameters exerting the strongest influence on simulation outcomes, carrying the greatest physical risk, and lacking adequate evidence, thereby reducing unnecessary user interaction while safeguarding physical fidelity. Stage gating mechanisms enforce rigorous checkpoints assessing whether accumulated evidence meets minimum requirements before advancing to subsequent phases. On 315 benchmark cases, GPT-5.5 achieves 99.4% execution success and 99.4% physical fidelity. A complex SUBOFF submarine case confirms the framework’s ability to orchestrate the full workflow, from model development and validation through geometry, meshing, parallel computation, and reporting. These results demonstrate that VibeFlow advances CFD automation toward a reproducible, auditable, and human-collaborative research paradigm, with further details and resources available at vibeflow.org.cn
ER  - 
